      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{62625e70171465529bd81f21|full_name}: I believe you are mistaken.  The operation of FFR can be visually subtle (which is the intent), and that can make it difficult to distinguish whether it is actually operating or not.\nI have re-run my testing to verify that FFR is not working.  Especially I have tested that the frame rate does not improve when FFR is enabled which is the most definitive way of determining whether it is actually operating.  When it used to function prior to the EAC release, it produced a 59% improvement in frame rate on VRChat on large FOV at 100% resolution in my tests.  That's hard to miss.\nI am using Pitool 1.0.1.280.  FFR was definitely working before the EAC release and is definitely not working afterward.  I'm confident that no version of Pitool including 277 makes FFR work right now.  The feature has always relied on DLL injection.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
